---
export const title = 'Mentions';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The editors store a mention as a Markdown link with the <code>mention:</code>
  scheme: the trigger and name as the link text, the id as the address. It
  reads well in any Markdown viewer, and <code>wc-markdown</code> shows it as a
  chip.
</p>

<pre><code>[@Ana Lima](mention:usr_142)</code></pre>

<p>
  Set <code>mention-href</code> to make mentions links. <code>{'{id}'}</code>
  is replaced by the mention's id.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-markdown
    mention-href="#user-{id}"
    value="Restarted the worker. [@Ana Lima](mention:usr_142), can you verify on [#INC-2041](mention:inc_2041)?"
  ></wc-markdown>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3 class="text-title-medium">Finding who to notify</h3>

<p>
  <code>extractMentions(markdown)</code>, exported from
  <code>@redvars/peacock</code>, lists the mentions in a value once each,
  skipping code. Use it when a comment is saved to decide who to notify.
</p>

<pre><code>import {'{ extractMentions }'} from '@redvars/peacock';

extractMentions('Thanks [@Ana Lima](mention:usr_142)!');
// [{'{ id: \'usr_142\', label: \'Ana Lima\', trigger: \'@\' }'}]</code></pre>
